:Bridge a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Bridge"@en ;
    dcterms:modified "2025-01-30"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-03-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "It is a structure constructed for the exclusive purpose of carrying railroad traffic across an obstruction. It can be used for defining non-stopping areas, big metal mass, resistance to traffic load etc."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :InfrastructureElement ;
    owl:disjointWith :HABD,
        :KilometricPost,
        :LevelCrossing,
        :OperationalPoint,
        :PlatformEdge,
        :PrimaryLocation,
        :RadioBlockCenter,
        :RunningTrack,
        :SectionOfLine,
        :Siding,
        :Signal,
        :SpecialArea,
        :Switch,
        :Track,
        :Tunnel .

:LinearElementSection a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Linear Element Section"@en ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/LinearElementSectionShape> ;
    rdfs:comment "Represents a section of a linear element."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :LinearElement ;
    skos:scopeNote "A linear element section is a finer granularity of a linear element, representing a specific portion of it. This concept is introduced to address the cases when a linear element needs to be split such as a part of it is used by a net referencing (more in the paragraph describing the positioning on the network). By using start and end offsets measured from origin of the element in ascending order, sections eliminate the need for intrinsic coordinates and instead rely on distances along the linear element."@en .

:NetLinearReference a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Net Linear Reference"@en ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/NetLinearReferenceShape> ;
    dcterms:created "2024-11-29"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Represents a linear reference in the network."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :NetBasicReference ;
    skos:example "Example: tracks, tunnels, bridges, platform edges etc."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "It is used for infrastructure elements positioned in relation to the topology as a line, or along a path. (e.g.: tracks, bridges, platform edges, etc.)"@en .

:accelerationLevelCrossing a owl:FunctionalProperty,
        owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Acceleration allowed near level crossing"@en ;
    :XMLName "IHS_AccelerationLevelCrossing" ;
    :applicable "Y/N" ;
    :dependencyNote "Mandatory value when the level crossing is defined"@en ;
    :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.7.3" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/AccelerationLevelCrossing>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/AccelerationLevelCrossingApplicability> ;
    dcterms:created "2021-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2024-01-08"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-11-20"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Existence of limit for acceleration of train if stopping or recovering speed close to a level crossing expressed in a specific reference acceleration curve."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :Track ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :Track ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :Track ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :Track ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :Track ) ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range :Document ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :healthSafetyAndEnvironmentObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """The value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document.
If a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the "Reference Documents Management" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document.
If an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."""@en .

:carrierLinearElement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "carrier linear element"@en ;
    dcterms:created "2025-01-30"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "The carrier linear element in relation to which the orientation is based on"@en ;
    rdfs:domain :Orientation ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range :LinearElement .

:ccsSubsystemDeclarationsVerificationTrackObjParameter a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Declarations of verification for track"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.1" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :ccsSubsystemObjParameter .

:conditionsSwitchClassBSystems a owl:FunctionalProperty,
        owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Special technical conditions required to switch over between ERTMS/ETCS and Class B systems"@en ;
    :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
    :dependencyNote "Applicable when at least two different class of protection systems exist."@en ;
    :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
    :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.8.3",
        "1.2.1.1.7.3" ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsSwitchClassBSystems>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ConditionsSwitchClassBSystemsApplicability> ;
    :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.3" ;
    dcterms:created "2022-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date,
        "2024-11-04"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:relation :ETCS,
        :switchProtectControlWarning ;
    dcterms:source <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2019/773/oj>,
        <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the Special technical conditions required to switch over between ERTMS/ETCS and Class B systems."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range :Document ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :transitionsBetweenSystemsObjParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """The details of the conditions to switch between Class B train protection systems must be published.

The value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document.
If a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the "Reference Documents Management" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document.
If an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."""@en .

:contactLineSystem a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "contact line system"@en ;
    :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/ContactLineSystem> ;
    dcterms:created "2020-08-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified "2021-09-11"^^xsd:date,
        "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "System that is used to transmit electrical energy to road or rail vehicles."@en ;
    rdfs:domain [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ],
        [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset :RunningTrack ) ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range :ContactLineSystem ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """It can be repeated as many times as the number of different contact line system types are present.

For RDF data provision:
The value of this property is an instance of the era:ContactLineSystem, which has as properties the parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2, 1.1.1.2.2.2, 1.1.1.2.2.4 and 1.1.1.2.5.1.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, this property is the equivalent of the "Set" attribute, grouping parameters 1.1.1.2.2.1.2, 1.1.1.2.2.2, 1.1.1.2.2.4 and 1.1.1.2.5.1."""@en .

:dataGSMRNetwork a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "Data GSM-R network"@en ;
    :eratvIndex "4.13.2.11" ;
