    rdfs:comment """If the trackside does not provide Track Conditions, the driver will need to be informed about such conditions via alternative methods.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en ;
    rdfs:domain :ETCS ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.era.europa.eu/domains/technical-specifications-interoperability/control-command-and-signalling-tsi_en#oe-content-paragraph-1632"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :tsiCompliantTrainProtectionSystemDataParameter ;
    ns1:term_status "stable" ;
    skos:scopeNote """According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]
If the trackside does not provide Track Conditions, the driver will need to be informed about such conditions via alternative methods.
In ETCS level NTC and level 0 track conditions are not managed (at least in Baseline 2)
See: TSI CCS (Subset-026, Chapter 5, section 5.18)"""@en .

